#: ../../source/index.rst:39
#: de824c2869e54166a66dd8fcb1cff495
msgid ":ref:`Hardware <stores>`  is the peripheral sensors, controller, and output devices that act as the vehicle's eyes, ears, brain and arms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:42
#: 85859a192b07488ea90046ce32a98bce
msgid "Almost any mobile machine can be transformed into an autonomous vehicle, by simply integrating a small hardware package into it. Hardware packages begin with a controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:46
#: 22516ee5f4ba44dc93e9eed420df73fb
msgid "Using inputs from sensors, the controller is able to send outputs to devices such as ESC's, servos, gimbals and other peripherals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:60
#: 3bf5650516e24fc19e8959bce5970abf
msgid ":ref:`Firmware <common-downloads_firmware>` is the code running on the controller. You choose the firmware to match your vehicle and mission: :ref:`Copter <copter:home>`, `Plane <https://ardupilot.org/plane/index.html>`__, :ref:`Rover <rover:home>`, Sub, or :ref:`Antenna Tracker <antennatracker:home>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:64
#: 7287bcbc02b340ceb6689a1ca9215f3d
msgid "The choice is yours -- one autopilot for any mission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:77
#: 41c98d1074104ca6a836edc688219b06
msgid ":ref:`Ground Control Station <common-choosing-a-ground-station>` (GCS) is your interface to the controller. Various versions of GCS software are available for Window's, Linux, and Android platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:80
#: 5a5624caacb84a4ebd9dc93bbe0b41df
msgid "A GCS allows users to set-up, configure, test, and tune the vehicle. Advanced packages allow autonomous mission planning, operation, and post-mission analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:84
#: c086d56800424edcb2f104a21726c830
msgid ":ref:`Mission Planner <planner:home>` is a full-featured GCS supported by ArduPilot. It offers point-and-click interaction with your hardware, custom scripting, and simulation."
msgstr ""

